{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"that person logan","id":"519566652824616973","is_bot":0,"username":"thatpersonlogan"},"author_id":"519566652824616973","channel_id":"733827680490881095","content":"*”Wren! Come here, or you’ll miss supper!” Paya Rosewood calls out from the back door of the small cottage. Wren is smaller here, maybe 6 or 7. She carries a small bow on her back and is holding a large rabbit in each hand. She runs up to the woman, “Mama! Mama! I did it! I caught my first giant hare!” Paya smiles down at her only child. “I’m so proud of you” she says with a smile. She means it. A tall man follows her out of the woods. He nods at Wren, then at Paya, “she needs more practice.” He walks into the house without another word. Payas face is no longer smiling. She holds Wren tighter, “I love you” she whispers into Wrens bright hair* the memory fades","created_at":"2020-08-21T02:54:34.652000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"746200549145182248","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
